{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1034490-help-creating-npc-mage-that-works-for-a-vampire","id":1034490,"title":"Help Creating NPC Mage that Works for a Vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-19T02:19:44-08:00","id":1034490,"title":"Help Creating NPC Mage that Works for a Vampire","content":"In my campaign I have a gangster Nosferatu Anarch who is one of the opponents a mixed PC group of mages and vampires are facing. The gangster vampire is looking for a bit of additional firepower and would like to recruit a mage to assist with countering the PCs.<br /> <br /> My initial idea was to have a mercenary Life and Mind mage (plus supporting spheres) who was also a Ghoul, however I liked that idea so much that I've decided to play it as a character next time I'm in a Mage game.<br /> <br /> This means I'm now stuck for ideas for a Mage who would be useful at supporting the gangster and a bunch of newly embraced fledglings. I thought maybe someone with Forces for some literal firepower (especially as the PC mage are all pretty subtle) but it seems a bit vulgar - any Mage throwing around a lot of Vulgar Magick is soon goon to be out of the running.<br /> <br /> Anyone got any better ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T03:31:38-08:00","id":1034507,"title":"","content":"First of all, what does the Nosferatu use the Mage for? Spying, bodyguard, assassin, companionship, source of money, some thing else?<br /> Second of all, what is the Mages Paradigm? How does Magick work for him, how does he view his magic? How does he view the world?<br /> Thirdly, what type of abilities and other stats does the character have?<br /> Lastly, what are the mages Spheres?<br /> <br /> Answer the questions in that order and you should be able to think of something in no time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: For ideas, perhaps a goon or hired gun that has learned to enchant his bullets for more devastating effects (Prime 2 for just agg, Forces 2 or 3 for Fire/Ice effects on impact or just an explosive bullet, Correspondance 2+Life 2 to make sure that the bullets never miss).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":392,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","user":"Cadmiumcadamium","date":". 01-19-2017, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:24:45-08:00","id":1034653,"title":"","content":"Mages should never be retainers, they are just too versatile, and should be a valued friend. A Mage ally should be someone that the Kindred treasures because they have found a Mage who sees them as something more than a Tass factory. A particularly useful Mage for Kindred would be a Kindred healer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:48:23-08:00","id":1034712,"title":"","content":"If you want it to a be a mage bound through viniculum why don't you just go with a Tremere? It's far more believable one of their kind would be bound due to their clan weakness, and they can be just as helpful. A Tremere would add to the tension considering their clan history and they are very much a threat to human mages due to how nightfolk counter-magick works. <br /> <br /> Most mortal mages powerful enough to get the attention of a Vampire would probably know that you lose your avatar when you become one of the undead, so they'd be wary working with or for them. It would be a tense relationship at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:02:07-08:00","id":1034804,"title":"","content":"If you want to use a Mage agent, it matters what the Nosferatu needs the Mage's talents for. This will, in turn, shape what kind of Mage they'd hire. Nosferatu are stereotyped by their inability to unwillingness to deal with people. It's difficult to practice social skills when you live in a sewer and look like a monster, even if the latter can be disguised with Obfuscate. Rather than merely being magical muscle, the Mage could be a smooth-talking negotiator. They understand people enough to influence them, and thereby get them on the boss's side. And since the Mage is mortal, they can operate at times and in circles a vampire can't.<br /> <br /> In M20 terms, a character who uses the extremely subtle Art of Desire. Or perhaps...Hypereconomics.<br /> <br /> Consider using a Syndicate Enforcer. The methodology has plentiful experience working in organized crime, and can serve both as a negotiator and in a combat capacity. Syndicate reps also, like all Technocrats, have a vested interest in maintaining the Consensus, a point they have in common with Masquerade-minded vampires.<br /> <br /> This idea has the added benefit of complicating the relationship between the Nos and the Enforcer. While the vampire may grasp on some level that their &quot;employee&quot; wields more than just good people skills, they won't know that the Enforcer is in the same class of being as a wizard. To the Nos, the Syndicate rep is a well-connected, knowledgeable man of some means, with the intel and technology to match the efforts of these mysterious PC mystics. The Nos is put in a position where he must rely on the Enforcer's skills and expertise, while not being able to fully trust him (that is, less so than vampires are in the habit of trusting anyone). On the Syndicate rep's side, he sees the vampire as not just a source of money, contact in the underworld, and a means of enforcing the Consensus, but also a doorway into the enigmatic world of hemovores. Walk with the parasite, and you'll come to understand the world of parasites. Given that the Technocracy isn't aware of just all that goes on among the blood-suckers (else they'd realize how close the lot of them come to breaking the &quot;Masquerade&quot; wide open at any given time, and thus need to be destroyed), it's to their benefit to have someone on the inside, gathering intelligence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:09:40-08:00","id":1035321,"title":"","content":"Bluecho thank you that sounds like an excellent fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}